(no_connect (at 152.4 116.84) (uuid dc625a8e-e9c0-4062-88bd-87baa88f80d3))
(text "PHYSICAL HARNESS PATH\nFactory transmission wiring -> Ford J1 -> new PCB J120\n-> short internal pigtail -> shell J121 -> cabin cable\n-> MicroSquirt V3 35-way AMPSEAL.\n\nJ120 cavity n mates to J121 cavity n electrically.\nMicroSquirt cavity numbers DIFFER: use the harness table.\nJ121 is off-board; omit from PCB placement.\n\nThe cabin cable carries solenoid CURRENT as well as\nsensor signals, power/returns and CAN. It is not a\nCAN-only or ribbon-cable connection.\n\nTwist CAN H/L together; route VR speed as a pair.\nKeep solenoid PWM currents out of sensor-return wiring.\nProvide strain relief and a sealed cable route.\nA shell opening is distinct from a firewall opening." (at 220 47 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid a91023cf-e508-5215-b080-2a5e0e75bd36))
(text "J121 contact rating, conductor sizes, terminal seals, cable length and shell cutout are not yet selected.\nPins 17, 19 and 20 have no assigned MicroSquirt signal endpoint; isolate/seal unused cabin contacts.\nMount the complete MicroSquirt inside the car, with its tuning connector accessible.\nThis change preserves the planned factory connector routes; it does not resolve the prior range/speed/ground review items." (at 15 219 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left top)) (uuid f75a027c-2b87-533f-b00a-70bdaa125930))
)